# 🏠 NYC Airbnb Data Analysis (Task 3 - Oasis Infobyte Internship)

## 📌 Project Overview
This project is part of my **Oasis Infobyte Internship - Task 3**.

The objective is to analyze the NYC Airbnb dataset to understand listing patterns, pricing behavior, and distribution across neighborhoods.  
The project includes **data cleaning using Python** and **data visualization using Excel dashboards**.

---

## 🎯 Objective
- Clean and preprocess raw Airbnb dataset  
- Handle missing values and incorrect data types  
- Perform exploratory data analysis (EDA)  
- Create meaningful visualizations using Excel  
- Understand listing patterns across NYC  

---

## 🛠️ Tools & Technologies Used
- Python (Pandas, NumPy) – Data Cleaning  
- Kaggle Notebook – Data Processing  
- Microsoft Excel – Data Visualization  
- Kaggle Dataset – NYC Airbnb Open Data  

---

## 📊 Dataset Description
The dataset includes Airbnb listing information such as:

- Listing ID  
- Host ID  
- Neighborhood Group  
- Neighborhood  
- Room Type  
- Price  
- Minimum Nights  
- Number of Reviews  
- Availability  

---

## 🧹 Data Cleaning (Python)

The following preprocessing steps were performed:

- Imported dataset using Pandas  
- Checked and handled missing values  
- Removed duplicate records  
- Fixed incorrect data types  
- Filtered out unrealistic values (outliers in price)  
- Standardized categorical columns (room type, neighborhood group)  
- Exported cleaned dataset for further analysis  

---

## 📈 Data Visualization (Excel)

The cleaned dataset was imported into Excel for visualization.  
The following dashboards and charts were created:

- Room Type Distribution (Bar Chart)  
- Price Distribution Analysis (Histogram)  
- Neighborhood Group Analysis  
- Reviews Count Analysis  
- Availability Analysis  
- KPI Cards (Total Listings, Average Price, Total Reviews)  

